# =============================================================================
# Hello Darzi — Environment Configuration
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# =============================================================================

# SHARED ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (used by all platforms)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-key"
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-key"

# WEB APPLICATION (apps/website)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_ prefix is required by Vite to expose to browser code.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-key"

# DESKTOP APPLICATION (apps/desktop)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to "true" when running in Electron with local SQLite database.
# ELECTRON_RUN="true"

# GOOGLE OAUTH (reference only — configured in Supabase dashboard)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are for documentation purposes only. The actual Google OAuth
# configuration happens in Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers.
# The desktop app does NOT need a separate Google OAuth client — it uses
# Supabase as the OAuth intermediary.

# Web Client ID used by Supabase Google provider
# WEB_CLIENT="your-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com"

# DATABASE MIGRATIONS — Direct PostgreSQL Connection
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for automatic schema migrations on Supabase.
# Get the connection string from Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → Database.
# Example:
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.vecwyofzniisruyxnzwe:password@aws-0-ap-southeast-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres"
# DATABASE_URL=""

# VERCEL BUILD — GitHub Token
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required in Vercel environment variables (not needed locally).
# Used by build.mjs to fetch the latest GitHub release for the download button.
# Create a classic token at https://github.com/settings/tokens with "repo" scope.
# GITHUB_TOKEN="ghp_your-token"

# =============================================================================
# Required Google Cloud Console & Supabase Configuration
# =============================================================================
#
# 1. GOOGLE CLOUD CONSOLE SETUP
#    Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#    Create or select a project.
#
#    1a. OAuth Consent Screen:
#        - User Type: External
#        - App Name: Hello Darzi
#        - User Support Email: your-email
#        - Developer Contact: your-email
#        - Scopes: email, profile, openid
#        - Test users: Add your email for development
#
#    1b. Create Web Client (for website):
#        - Authorized JavaScript origins:
#          http://localhost:3000
#          https://hellodarzi.shop
#          https://your-vercel-preview.vercel.app
#        - Authorized redirect URIs:
#          http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#          https://hellodarzi.shop/auth/callback
#          https://your-vercel-preview.vercel.app/auth/callback
#
#    1c. Create Desktop Client (for Electron):
#        - Application type: Desktop app
#        - Name: Hello Darzi Desktop
#        - Authorized redirect URIs:
#          hellodarzi://auth/callback
#
#    1d. Copy the Client ID and Client Secret for each.
#
# 2. SUPABASE DASHBOARD SETUP
#    Go to https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/YOUR_PROJECT/auth/providers
#
#    2a. Enable Google Provider:
#        - Client ID: Paste the Web Client ID from Google Cloud
#        - Client Secret: Paste the Web Client Secret
#        - Redirect URL will be auto-generated by Supabase
#          (e.g., https://vecwyofzniisruyxnzwe.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback)
#
#    2b. Copy this Supabase Redirect URL and add it to your Google Cloud
#        Console's Authorized redirect URIs.
#
# 3. DEEP LINK / CUSTOM PROTOCOL (Desktop only)
#    The desktop app registers the "hellodarzi://" protocol.
#    - Windows: Auto-registered by electron-builder in the NSIS installer.
#    - The OAuth flow opens the system browser, then Supabase redirects
#      back to hellodarzi://auth/callback with the session tokens.
#    - The OS delivers this URL to the app, which captures it and sets
#      the session.
#
# 4. WEBSITE OAUTH FLOW
#    The static marketing site uses Supabase's built-in OAuth redirect flow.
#    User clicks "Continue with Google" → redirected to Google →
#    redirected back to /auth/callback → session stored in localStorage.
